{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-83344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform of $y(t),$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}} & =L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's introduce $L{y}=Y(s).$ \n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{″}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}L{y}-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}Y(s).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}} & =L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-83344" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83344" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{2{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+4)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{{s}^{2}+2}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{{s}^{2}+4}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{2}{s({s}^{2}+2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+4)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83344" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+4)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform of $y(t),$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=1,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y} & =L{1} \\\\ L{{y}^{″}}-L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's introduce $L{y}=Y(s).$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}}$ and $L{{y}^{″}},$  we use formulas for the Laplace transforms of the derivatives and apply the initial conditions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}} & =sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s) \\\\ L{{y}^{″}} & ={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}-L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =L{1} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s)-sY(s)-2Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s+1)(s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s(s+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-83349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{(s+1)(s-2)}{s}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s+1)(s-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+s+1)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{(s+1)(s-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{s(s+1)(s-2)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s+1)(s-2)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-102398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform of $y(t),$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4y={e}^{-t},\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-102398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}-4y} & =L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\ L{{y}^{″}}-4L{y} & =L{{e}^{-t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's introduce $L{y}=Y(s).$ \n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{″}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}L{y}-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}={s}^{2}Y(s)-1.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{e}^{-t}}=\\frac{1}{s+1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}-4L{y} & =L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}Y(s)-1)-4Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-4)Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+1}+1 \\\\ ({s}^{2}-4)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{(s+1)({s}^{2}-4)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{(s+1)(s-2)(s+2)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{(s+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-102398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-102398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-102398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{(s+1)(s-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{2(s+1)^{2}}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{4(s-2)^{2}}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{4}{(s+1)^{2}}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s-2)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-102398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{(s+1)(s-2)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-64442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s\\ge \\sqrt{2}$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2y={t}^{2},\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-64442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}-2y} & =L{{t}^{2}} \\\\ L{{y}^{″}}-2L{y} & =L{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{″}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}L{y}-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}Y(s)-2.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}-2L{y} & =L{{t}^{2}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}Y(s)-2)-2Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-2)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{3}+1)}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{3}+1)}{{s}^{3}({s}^{2}-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-64442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-64442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-64442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{2({s}^{3}+1)}{{s}^{3}({s}^{2}-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{2({s}^{3}+2)}{{s}^{3}({s}^{2}-1)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}({s}^{2}-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{3}+1}{s({s}^{2}-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{3}}{{s}^{2}-1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-64442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{2({s}^{3}+1)}{{s}^{3}({s}^{2}-2)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform of $y(t),$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=t,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}} & =L{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's introduce $L{y}=Y(s).$ \n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{″}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}L{y}-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}Y(s)-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}} & =L{t} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s)-1 & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+1 \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-83345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{3}}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{4}}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{3}+1}{{s}^{4}}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{4}+1}{{s}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-83345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{4}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)+y(t)=7,\\,y(0)=7,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s)=\\frac{7(1+{s}^{2})}{s}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s) & =\\frac{7(1+{s}^{2})}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{7(1+{s}^{2})}{s} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{7}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>0.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{7}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =7{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-345083" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345083" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)-4y(t)=-4,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)-s-4Y(s)=-\\frac{4}{s}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-s-4Y(s) & =-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-4)Y(s) & =s-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-4)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{s} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{s({s}^{2}-4)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>2.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-345076" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345076" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)+y(t)=2{t}^{4}+24{t}^{2},\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s)=\\frac{48(1+{s}^{2})}{{s}^{5}}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s) & =\\frac{48(1+{s}^{2})}{{s}^{5}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{48(1+{s}^{2})}{{s}^{5}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{48}{{s}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>0.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{48}{{s}^{5}}} \\\\ y(t) & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}} \\\\ y(t) & =2{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-345084" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345084" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2t^4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-9y=-8{e}^{-t},\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)-2s-2-9Y(s)=-\\frac{8}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-2s-2-9Y(s) & =-\\frac{8}{s+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-9)Y(s) & =2s+2-\\frac{8}{s+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-9)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+2s-3)}{s+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-9)Y(s) & =\\frac{2(s+3)(s-1)}{s+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2(s+3)(s-1)}{(s+1)(s-3)(s+3)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2(s-1)}{(s+1)(s-3)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>3.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-3}} \\\\ y(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}} \\\\ y(t) & ={e}^{-t}+{e}^{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-345078" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345078" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{-t}+e^{3t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)-y(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)-1-Y(s)=-2(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}).\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-1-Y(s) & =-2(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}) \\\\ ({s}^{2}-1)Y(s) & =1-\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-1)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-1}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>1.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bb1f7104001b3a99915af7f8bf00915e4b11cc32da4527c119ec0f2a54c0418"} {"question" "q-345071" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "q-345071" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sin(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f23bece210a4b982c76fc1caf23c0fe918e1568580dace709e7f8fa73959f5b"} {"question" "e-6663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y(t)\\right\\}$ for $s\\geq\\sqrt5$ if \n\n$$\ny'' - 5y = 4e^{-3t}, \\quad y(0)=2, \\quad y'(0)=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/example-6663.json" "file_sha256" "2a84b889aff154e9d9744e5aaa21308336962878d12c8874cfaa7e2e1b79647a"} {"question" "e-6663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}-5y} & =L{4{e}^{-3t}} \\\\ L{{y}^{″}}-5L{y} & =4L{{e}^{-3t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y\\right\\}-sy(0)-y'(0)=s^2Y(s)-sy(0)-y'(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2Y(s)-2s+1.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{e^{-3t}\\right\\}=\\dfrac{1}{s+3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}-5L{y} & =4L{{e}^{-3t}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}Y(s)-2s+1)-5Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{s+3} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-5)Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{s+3}+2s-1 \\\\ ({s}^{2}-5)Y(s) & =\\frac{4+(2s-1)(s+3)}{s+3} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-5)Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+5s+1}{s+3} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+5s+1}{(s+3)({s}^{2}-5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/example-6663.json" "file_sha256" "2a84b889aff154e9d9744e5aaa21308336962878d12c8874cfaa7e2e1b79647a"} {"question" "e-6666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $y(t)$ if the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\ny'' +  6y = 2\\sin {2t}, \\quad y(0) = 0, \\quad y'(0) = 2\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\ns^2Y(s) - 2 +6 Y(s)  =  2\\left(\\dfrac{2}{s^2 + 4}\\right).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/example-6666.json" "file_sha256" "de518a1a69f7298d119ef527be8291db4c10e4a18c15cc6515af7240020506bb"} {"question" "e-6666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-2+6Y(s) & =2(\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}), \\\\ ({s}^{2}+6)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+6)Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+12}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+6)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+6)}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{Y(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y(t) =  \\sin {2t}$ is the solution of the original differential equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073514/example-6666.json" "file_sha256" "de518a1a69f7298d119ef527be8291db4c10e4a18c15cc6515af7240020506bb"}] "usage" {"q-345071" [] "q-64442" [] "e-6663" [] "e-6666" []} "basis" 2702 "retractions" [[17592186148100 :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s) = L{y(t)}$ for $s \\ge \\sqrt{2}$ if\n\n$y^{″} - 2y = t^{2}, y(0) = 0, y^{′}(0) = 2$."] [17592186147736 :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n$y^{″}(t) - y(t) =-2\\sin t, y(0) = 0, y^{′}(0) = 1$\n\nis given by\n\n$s^{2}Y(s) - 1 - Y(s) =-2(\\frac{1}{s^{2} + 1})$.\n\nThe solution is $y(t) =$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186147305 :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y(t)\\right\\}$ for $s\\geq\\sqrt5$ if\n$y'' - 5y = 4e^{-3t}, \\quad y(0)=2, \\quad y'(0)=-1$."] [17592186147305 :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{y^{″} - 5y} &= L{4e^{-3t}} \\\\\nL{y^{″}} - 5L{y} &= 4L{e^{-3t}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwe use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y\\right\\}-sy(0)-y'(0)=s^2Y(s)-sy(0)-y'(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2Y(s)-2s+1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{e^{-3t}\\right\\}=\\dfrac{1}{s+3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{y^{″}} - 5L{y} &= 4L{e^{-3t}} \\\\\n(s^{2}Y(s) - 2s + 1) - 5Y(s) &= \\frac{4}{s + 3} \\\\\n(s^{2} - 5)Y(s) &= \\frac{4}{s + 3} + 2s - 1 \\\\\n(s^{2} - 5)Y(s) &= (4 + (2s - 1)(s + 3))/(s + 3) \\\\\n(s^{2} - 5)Y(s) &= \\frac{2s^{2} + 5s + 1}{s + 3} \\\\\nY(s) &= (2s^{2} + 5s + 1)/((s + 3)(s^{2} - 5))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186147306 :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ if the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n$y'' + 6y = 2\\sin {2t}, \\quad y(0) = 0, \\quad y'(0) = 2$\n\nis given by\n\n$s^2Y(s) - 2 +6 Y(s) = 2\\left(\\dfrac{2}{s^2 + 4}\\right)$."] [17592186147306 :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ns^{2}Y(s) - 2 + 6Y(s) &= 2(\\frac{2}{s^{2} + 4}), \\\\\n(s^{2} + 6)Y(s) &= 2 + \\frac{4}{s^{2} + 4} \\\\\n(s^{2} + 6)Y(s) &= \\frac{2s^{2} + 12}{s^{2} + 4} \\\\\n(s^{2} + 6)Y(s) &= (2(s^{2} + 6))/(s^{2} + 4) \\\\\nY(s) &= \\frac{2}{s^{2} + 4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\nL{\\sin 2t} = \\frac{2}{s^{2} + 4}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{Y(s)} &= L^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s^{2} + 4}} \\\\\ny(t) &= \\sin 2t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\ny(t) = \\sin {2t}\n$$\n\nis the solution of the original differential equation."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186146612 17592186146613 17592186146614 17592186146615 17592186146616] "immutable_fields" [[17592186144407 :answer-field/id] [17592186144407 :answer-field/key] [17592186144407 :answer-field/type] [17592186146611 :answer-field/correct] [17592186146611 :answer-field/id] [17592186146611 :answer-field/key] [17592186146611 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
